  "final_output": "**Cause: Stripe is degraded.** From 11:20 UTC, Stripe POST /v1/payment_intents is slow and often returns HTTP 200 with an empty body. Payment cannot parse the empty body and returns 502, so Order fails the checkout.\n\n**Evidence**\n- third_party_health(stripe), 11:00 to 12:00: p95 latency reaches 9,791 ms (normal about 372 ms). The trace below shows one Stripe call of 6.8 s at 11:22. The Stripe error rate is 0%, because the responses are HTTP 200. That is why ThirdPartyErrors does not fire.\n- Trace aca55dbebae747f12388b76923472fac (order ord_8A9BF2): the stripe POST /v1/payment_intents span takes 6.8 s and returns 200 with body_bytes=0. Then parse stripe response fails with unexpected end of JSON input. Payment returns 502, Order returns 502, and Order releases the reserved stock. The Order spans themselves take a few milliseconds.\n- log_patterns(payment), 11:20 to 12:00: a new error, failed to parse stripe response, 191 times (0 in the 40 minutes before), with error unexpected end of JSON input and stripe_latency_ms of 5 to 10 s.\n\n**Not the cause: the Order v4.12.0 deploy at 11:16** (gift message field). The time is spent in the Payment to Stripe call, the new error is in Payment, which was not deployed, and GET /orders/:id on the new version has a p95 of 8 ms. Do not roll it back.\n\n**Impact (11:20 to 12:00 UTC, still ongoing)**\n- Checkout success is 38.7% of 1,182 attempts, and the lowest minute is 22%. About 725 checkouts did not succeed.\n- In the sampled failed checkouts, customers wait 5 to 10 s, then get a 502 error.\n- The fault is still active at 12:00. CheckoutSuccessLow, PaymentSuccessLow, and the Payment and Order error and latency alerts are still firing.\n\n**Do now**\n1. Check the Stripe status page and open a Stripe support ticket with the request IDs and times (from 11:20 UTC).\n2. Do not roll back Order.\n3. Watch checkout_success_rate and Stripe p95 latency until they return to normal. Tell support that customers can try